research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:3:The 2026-10-31 full-graph development run finished. Its R1/R2/R3/R5 marks pass; R4 fails (retained margin ratio 0.522180, required 0.70). This is not joint long-term-memory success. Six seeds, four associations, arbitrary assigned consequences, and a synthetic KC relay: no chess fact or biological timescale was learned.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:5:Original evidence: [summary](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-10-31/eye-graph-memory-v1/summary.json), [records](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-10-31/eye-graph-memory-v1/records.jsonl), [frozen specification](../memory-retention-continuation-2026-10-31/eye-graph-memory-spec.md). The original script and outcomes remain unchanged.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:7:The next comparison is specified in [cubic-exit-spec.md](cubic-exit-spec.md). Its outcome is pending. This is a bounded development iteration under the researcher's continuing memory instruction; it does not select a biological rule or authorize chess training.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:10:The original fixed comparison at `runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/eye-graph-memory-cubic-v1` was interrupted and remains preserved. Its active continuation is `runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/eye-graph-memory-cubic-v1-recovery1`, through [the recovery registration](../../../python%20actions/eye-memory-cubic-v1-recovery1-step.json). Do not relaunch either path. [Independent original-result audit](v1-audit.json) confirms the delay failure. [First informative-arm replay](first-arm-audit.json) passes 1240 local observations / 120 trials; its within-seed delay ratio is .756635 versus the original same-seed .561696. This is not the six-seed gate result. [Regression verification](regression-verification.json): 745/751 pass, with the exact six historical failures; five original focused checks pass separately.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:12:[Separately researched molecular stabilization lead](molecular-stabilization-lead.md): primary Orb2 timing evidence and a published aggregation model, with explicit compartment/reversibility gaps; not an implementation or a retroactive source for cubic exit.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:15:**Second informative seed contradicts a general memory-success claim:** in seed 4102, reversing one association makes an unrelated old association incorrect (margin .140130 to -.020325). Another old margin falls to .058572 from .283405. A later pooled median pass cannot erase these failures. The full six-seed run continues unchanged. [Local replay of seed 4102](second-informative-arm-audit.json), [input-overlap description of the first two informative seeds](input-overlap-first-seed.json). Shared cells are a hypothesis for interference, not a proven cause or a tested five-cell repair.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:17:Recovery is verified: [336-update checkpoint replay](checkpoint-verification.json) and [53 actual resumed observations plus seven policy choices](resumed-overlap-verification.json) match the original valid stream exactly. Eight focused recovery/memory checks pass. The new owner was verified outside a Windows job, using the existing breakaway launcher. Source timing/RSS and resumed-invocation timing/RSS remain separate. [Recovery specification](recovery-spec.md), [original interruption evidence](interruption-evidence.json), [lineage](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/eye-graph-memory-cubic-v1-recovery1/recovery.json). Monitor with `fly.cmd --config "python actions/eye-memory-cubic-v1-recovery1-step.json" status`; run its independent audit after the summary is published. No memory equation or scientific gate changed.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:20:[Static readout/interference diagnostic](readout-interference-diagnostic.md): six direct-input surrogate comparisons yield no incapacity certificate, but do not establish feasibility of the full graph. [Raw static result](direct-input-surrogate-first-seeds.json). Before choosing another memory/input change, the next bounded graph question is whether the lost association remains lost when read against the circuit's current resting response. That diagnostic has not run and must wait for the serial controlled experiment.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:23:The 27-pass frozen-memory decoder diagnostic is now implemented and [registered](../../../python%20actions/eye-readout-offset-v1-step.json), with 12 passing focused checks across memory, recovery and the new readout instruments. It has not run. Its job is guarded on the complete controlled-run summary and matching independent replay audit; original versus current-rest readouts will be compared without changing any memory or parameter. [Software checks](postmortem-software-tests.txt).
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:26:[Latest partial chart: all three available informative seeds](retention-partial-three-seeds.html), [numeric source](retention-partial-three-seeds.json), [third-seed local replay](third-informative-arm-audit.json). The remaining three seeds and full controlled-run audit are pending. The earlier first-seed chart is a dated narrower snapshot, not the cohort result.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:28:## Status correction 2026-11-09: recovered six-seed run
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:30:The statements above that the full six-seed run continues and that three seeds remain predate its recovered completion. The original manifest remains `running` and has no matching live process; its original `records.jsonl` has five entries and no summary. The recovery run manifest is `complete`, its summary covers seeds 4101–4106, and its records contain 24 arm rows. The full independent `audit.json` is still absent, so the run is complete but not fully audited. Recovery-invocation timing and memory use are not whole-run measurements. No new training or audit was launched for this correction.
research/reports/memory-retention-continuation-2026-11-01/README.md:34:The 27-pass frozen-memory decoder diagnostic described above as not yet run completed on 2026-11-01. Its [manifest](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/readout-offset-v1/manifest.json) is complete; the [result](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/readout-offset-v1/result.json) records 27 passes, no teaching events or persistent updates, unchanged memory and parameters, 7.87 seconds, and 177.44 MiB peak RSS. It reproduces all eight original margins within 1e-10. Seed 4102's post-reversal margin remains negative: -0.02032499 with the original rest and -0.01335925 with the current rest. This does not rescue the lost association or establish a memory improvement. The later [interference diagnosis](../memory-interference-diagnosis-2026-11-01/README.md#deliverables-and-interpretation-boundary) reports the same result. The earlier pending statement is preserved as a dated snapshot; no experiment code or gate changed.
