documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:3:**Status: APPROVED 2026-10-30, with the researcher's definition of reasoning (section 2). The read-only eye test (section 7) may run after the decoder check below. Training may not start until the memory rule (section 5) has separate approval. The numbers in section 7 may change only from the decoder check, before any graph data exists.** Old runs stay as "early development" history. Their results do not count as evidence for this plan. Background: [restart handoff](../../handoffs/restart-handoff-2026-10-30.md).
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:5:Numbers marked [choice] are engineering choices fixed before any data. They do not come from a source.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:7:**Researcher-directed revision, 2026-10-31:** replace the conversational name “Readout v1” with `neuron-reader` and follow section 4A below. Build and verify passive recording first; specify the move score jointly with the separately approved memory mechanism. The [design review](../../../research/reports/neuron-reader-design-review-2026-10-31/README.md) supplies the reasons. The [exact plan before this revision](../../../research/reports/neuron-reader-design-review-2026-10-31/restart-plan-before-neuron-reader-update.md) is preserved. This revision changes the reader work order and contracts, not the numerical experiment gates, Eyes v1, memory selection or experiment permissions. The unresolved F03/F04 corrections remain separate pre-data decisions.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:15:The thesis under test: **the Fly first learns principles deeply, and later stages train reasoning on top of them.** Phase B (section 8) tests this directly. A success here is about this computer model. It does not show reasoning in a living fly.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:24:4. A simple learner with the same input and the same amount of practice fails on those positions.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:35:4. **Limit we disclose:** chess concepts all come from one game, so they are less unrelated than the researcher's example. A chess pass is evidence inside chess. It does not show the cross-domain ability in the example.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:41:1. Each photoreceptor looks at one square. We use Esposito's placement only (5,543 photoreceptors, 67-107 per square, stored in `.cache/full.npz`). We use none of his trained weights.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:58:5. **Not allowed:** hints, labels, teaching of moves it did not choose, showing the right move, repeating puzzles because of errors, or planning lessons from its errors. The puzzle order is fixed and hashed before training.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:72:2. **Pin the measurement.** Read each cell's final `model.h[model.steps][index]` after the existing finite-step rate dynamics. Copy these values before scratch arrays are reused. Keep every individual value and an arithmetic mean within each type; do not sum cell populations of unequal sizes. Record the model/snapshot hash, numerical precision, step count, normalization, recurrent scale, bias, leak and saturation. Use raw endpoint model-rate units: no fitted head, baseline subtraction, further clipping, data-fitted normalization or claim of Hz/biological duration.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:75:5. **Verify before graph use.** Software fixtures must establish exact roster selection, endpoint sampling, independent copied outputs, rejected invalid data, unchanged complete persistent state/board and candidate-order invariance under the same snapshot. Label fixture evidence separately from full-graph response. Reuse the existing simulator; no new learner, dependency or training mechanism is needed for recording.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:81:1. **Resolve each coefficient from evidence.** Record the source, exact cell/driver population, assay/manipulation, observed effect and limits. Behavioral valence, transmitter/fast-edge polarity, dopamine teaching sign and plasticity direction are different things. Unknown behavioral signs remain recorded with coefficient 0. Require at least one justified nonzero coefficient; do not fit coefficients to checker labels, Stockfish scores or sealed positions. A behavioral interpretation from a fly assay does not establish innate chess value.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:82:2. **Match the memory mechanism.** Check which observed cells the separately approved memory rule can actually change, and which model states it can reach. Verify that informative feedback can both raise and lower the relevant candidate margin against absent, matched-shuffled and disabled-plasticity controls in the separately declared memory test. Two numerical score signs are not required for ranking. If the reader misses needed memory targets, write an explicit revised roster and source rationale before data; do not silently add cells or alter the other session's mechanism.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:83:3. **Freeze the full chooser.** Before candidate-choice data, pin the nonzero coefficient table, equal type-mean pooling, score units, temperature, seed/PRNG, deterministic candidate ordering, tie/numerical tolerance and invalid-data behavior. Fix numeric values prospectively in the run manifest, not after seeing responses. Keep candidate preference distinct from calibrated position value. The section 7 supervised decoder is a diagnostic and does not supply the deployed score's coefficients.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:92:5. **After an eye-test pass, finalize the score with the separately approved memory rule.** Freeze the scalar/selection contract above and perform the separately approved real-route memory test. Informative feedback and matched controls must establish acquisition, retention and reversal before the existing chess training/transfer phases. Preserve the researcher approval boundary for the memory rule and the locked final tests. The source/target investigation can proceed earlier; this step is final selection, not a demand to stop the other session's development assays.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:96:**Not decided. We choose it only if the first test passes, and you approve it before training.**
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:106:5. **Hard rule.** No two-way rule enters training until the source register has its source, compartment and trigger. Any positive `D` must come from a modelled, source-backed trigger, not from the teacher.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:111:2. **Stop the floor with slow recovery.** Use the existing equation `dg = eta*D*(k+g-1)`, where inactive KCs recover toward 1 when dopamine fires. Old evidence: this erased a one-lesson trace in about 10 lessons. So each compartment gets its own recovery rate, fast in gamma and slow in alpha. Aso and Rubin support different rates per compartment, but give no numbers we can copy. The rates are a free choice and must be fixed on development data only.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:112:3. **Let real wires limit learning.** The graph has 480 direct MBON-to-dopamine edges. MBON14 to PPL106 (118 synapses) and MBON12 to PPL103 (102) are excitatory, so learning should lower the later dopamine and slow itself. MBON07 to PAM11 (83) is inhibitory, so learning should raise later dopamine; this may fit the consolidation loop in Ichinose et al. 2015. Today's pulse is at the top of its range (dopamine factors about -1), so these wires may have no room to act (hypothesis). Bennett et al. 2021 model this idea as prediction error. I read the abstract only, and their connections are partly proposed, not measured.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:114:5. **Test memory before chess.** Use simple non-chess patterns on the real graph. Measure how many associations it holds, interference, reversal and retention over many lessons, against the published behaviour in section 5.2. If this fails, we do not train on chess.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:144:2. Data: 48 new twin pairs from 48 unrelated training-pool games. In each pair the same capture is safe on one board and unsafe on the other. The old 12 pairs are too few (a false pass at 9/12 has a 7% chance). The old sealed sets stay closed.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:145:3. Decoder: L2 logistic regression, C = 1, standardized inputs [choice]. We train it with whole games left out. A pair is correct if the safe board scores above the unsafe board. Chance is 24/48.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:148:**Pre-data limitation recorded 2026-10-31:** item 4 is preserved as the original numerical gate, not silently repaired. The inspected old rules initialized at gain 1 cannot reach 1.8, and diagnostic decoder signs do not establish behavioral score signs. Its [F04 correction draft](../../../research/reports/overnight-memory-plasticity-2026-10-31/pre-data-corrections.md) remains unapplied. Resolve this separately before launch. An oracle gain/sign intervention can measure an engineering accessibility bound; it cannot validate the section 4A chooser, demonstrate endogenous learning or replace the frozen-memory diagnostic. This plan update changes no threshold or comparator pass rule.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:164:## 8. Locked test design and training phases
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:168:1. Made before any training, from games hash-split apart from the training pool. It excludes every game in old experiments.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:169:2. 60 twin pairs from 60 unrelated games: 30 use old pair kinds; 30 use **new kinds**, listed publicly now: a defender revealed by the capture; a defender that the capture itself blocks or removes; en passant recapture; a recapture only by the king; a recapture only by a promotion move.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:175:**Phase A (principle):** train with own-choice feedback on training-pool puzzles. Choose the snapshot using a separate development set only. Then freeze everything and run the locked test.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:177:**Phase B (the thesis):** only if Phase A passes. Before Phase B runs, you approve one addendum with a new task and its own locked set. Compare, at equal practice: Fly with Phase A memory; Fly starting fresh; Fly with Phase A exposure but shuffled feedback. **The thesis is supported only if the Phase A memory Fly beats both others on the new task's locked set.** If not, we report that the thesis failed in this test.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:183:3. Compare, at equal practice: the Fly with all concepts; each Fly with only one concept; a fresh Fly; a Fly with shuffled feedback; and the simple learner.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:193:3. **Better than every comparator:** at least 6 more pairs than each of arms 2-7, with the game-level bootstrap 95% lower limit above 0.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:195:5. **Retention:** with the snapshot frozen and the training set re-scored after all other training ends, no criterion falls more than 10% [choice].
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:242:6. New puzzle generator, new kinds, sealed test set.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:247:11. Public, dated pre-registration before data.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:248:12. Clean release: one command per figure; large raw data in a data archive.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:250:14. ISEF: the student explains every equation, discloses AI help, and checks the entry-year rules and any approval needed before data collection.
